  "body": "Stage 11 fixes one worker-slot recovery gap without changing normal browser reuse.\n\nFinding:\n- each BotWorkerSlot intentionally reuses one BrowserManager across jobs;\n- job exceptions are isolated correctly, but if the underlying Chromium process disconnects/crashes, the slot historically kept the same non-null BrowserManager;\n- later jobs could therefore keep trying to create contexts against a dead Browser and repeatedly fail even though the scheduler/thread itself remained alive.\n\nFix:\n- BrowserManager exposes an owner-thread-only `isHealthy()` check backed by Playwright `Browser.isConnected()`;\n- before a claimed job reuses the browser runtime, BotWorkerSlot checks that connection;\n- only a disconnected runtime is closed/discarded and replaced lazily with a fresh BrowserManager;\n- ordinary page timeouts, selector failures, backend errors and rate limits do not restart a healthy browser runtime.\n\nVerification:\n- the existing real Chromium encrypted-session smoke now asserts the BrowserManager health probe before and after context/session work.\n\nScope: 3 Playwright files only. No backend/database/frontend, selectors, target logic, quotas, guards, or real-action semantics changed.",
